From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:19:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 24/48] net: airoha: xpon: let Encrypted_Port-ID restore GEM
 ports OMCI created

"Encrypted_Port-ID must not create GEM ports" stopped the message from
validating Port-IDs nobody created. The field logs show one case where
that validation mattered, though: after a Deactivate_ONU-ID the Huawei
OLT sometimes provisions nothing over OMCI again but does repeat
Encrypted_Port-ID for every service port. Where the session start
resets the MAC (EN7523, gpon_reset_on_start) the GEM table is empty at
that point, and the Encrypted_Port-ID write is what made the service
ports valid again.

Track the GEM ports OMCI enabled and has not disabled in omci_gems,
which like the agent's MIB survives session restarts, and let
Encrypted_Port-ID put such a port back into the GEM table. A Port-ID
OMCI never created is still only recorded.

On the EN751221 the GEM table is not cleared between sessions (see
gpon_stop_clear_gems), so the field behaviour is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index dd10093..869cd7e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -2228,7 +2228,7 @@ static int gpon_cb_set_gem_encryption(void *hw_priv, u16 port_id,
 				      bool encrypted)
 {
 	struct xpon_priv *priv = hw_priv;
-	bool configured;
+	bool configured, restore;
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	if (port_id >= GPON_MAX_GEM_ID)
@@ -2250,9 +2250,19 @@ static int gpon_cb_set_gem_encryption(void *hw_priv, u16 port_id,
 	mutex_lock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
 	__assign_bit(port_id, priv->encrypted_gems, encrypted);
 	configured = test_bit(port_id, priv->hw_gems);
+	/*
+	 * A port OMCI created and has not deleted, but which is missing from
+	 * the GEM table (a MAC reset at session start on EN7523), is put back
+	 * as before: when the OLT skips OMCI provisioning after a reactivation
+	 * this message is what restores it.
+	 */
+	restore = !configured && test_bit(port_id, priv->omci_gems);
 	if (configured)
 		ret = gpon_write_gem_port_hw(priv, port_id, true, encrypted);
 	mutex_unlock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
+	if (restore)
+		ret = __gpon_set_gem_port_hw(priv, port_id, true, encrypted,
+					     true);
 
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(priv->dev,
@@ -2262,7 +2272,8 @@ static int gpon_cb_set_gem_encryption(void *hw_priv, u16 port_id,
 		dev_info(priv->dev,
 			 "GPON GEM encryption update: port=%u %s%s\n",
 			 port_id, encrypted ? "encrypted" : "clear",
-			 configured ? "" : " (recorded, port not created yet)");
+			 configured ? "" : restore ? " (OMCI port restored)" :
+			 " (recorded, port not created yet)");
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -2467,6 +2478,11 @@ int airoha_gpon_omci_hw_set_gem_port(void *hw_priv, u16 entity_id,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Survives session restarts, like the agent's MIB. */
+	mutex_lock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
+	__assign_bit(gem_port_id, priv->omci_gems, valid);
+	mutex_unlock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
+
 	gpon_refresh_netdev_link(priv, false);
 	dev_info(priv->dev,
 		 "OMCI GEM port %u %s (ME %#x T-CONT %#x direction %u)\n",
@@ -5216,6 +5232,7 @@ static int airoha_xpon_init_gpon(struct platform_device *pdev,
 					   priv, &gpon_lab_err_ctrl_fops);
 	bitmap_zero(priv->service_gems, GPON_MAX_GEM_ID);
 	bitmap_zero(priv->encrypted_gems, GPON_MAX_GEM_ID);
+	bitmap_zero(priv->omci_gems, GPON_MAX_GEM_ID);
 	memset(priv->tcont_alloc_id, 0xff, sizeof(priv->tcont_alloc_id));
 	memset(priv->tcont_entity_id, 0xff, sizeof(priv->tcont_entity_id));
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.h
index f720931..daed27d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.h
@@ -539,6 +539,8 @@ struct xpon_priv {
 	DECLARE_BITMAP(service_gems, GPON_MAX_GEM_ID);
 	/* GEM ports the OLT made encrypted with Encrypted_Port-ID (PLOAM) */
 	DECLARE_BITMAP(encrypted_gems, GPON_MAX_GEM_ID);
+	/* GEM ports OMCI created and has not deleted (gem_mib_lock) */
+	DECLARE_BITMAP(omci_gems, GPON_MAX_GEM_ID);
 
 	/*
 	 * Per-GEM MIB counters. gem_mib_lock serialises the MIB command
